message: "If you use this analysis or its code, please cite it as below."
title: "The Load Nobody Planned For: Weather-Adjusted Electricity Demand Growth Across U.S. Grids, 2016–2026"
authors:
  - family-names: Pospisil
    given-names: John
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-11-08
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/johnpospisil/datacenter-grid-load"
url: "https://johnpospisil.github.io/datacenter-grid-load/"
abstract: >-
  Hourly EIA-930 demand for 23 U.S. balancing authorities, weather-adjusted with
  per-region models fitted on 2016–2019 (ERA5 weather), shows structural growth
  since 2022 concentrated in data-center regions, led by PJM's Dominion zone
  (+24%), and added as a flat 24/7 floor. Data through 2026-10-22.
keywords:
  - electricity demand
  - data centers
  - weather normalization
  - EIA-930
  - power grid
